# SEG definition — SEG-WELD-01

[Established 2025-11-05](#established) by [R. Osei, CIH](#author). These
workers can be treated as one exposure group because they share
[the same task mix, ventilation regime, materials, and overlapping
shifts](#rationale) — the exposure determinants, not the org chart. Agents of
concern: [manganese](#agent-mn), [hexavalent chromium](#agent-cr6), and
[total welding fume](#agent-fume). Who is in the group and when:
[membership-rules.mdy](membership-rules.mdy).
